cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its record, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ripple Engine: a pre-registered, historically-conditioned engine for reading geopolitical shocks in the oil economy, with a sealed walk-forward test"
authors:
  - family-names: Delany
    given-names: Joseph
    email: joseph.delany21@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Colby College"
version: "2.5"
date-released: "2026-09-02"
repository-code: "https://github.com/josephdelany/ripple-engine"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - oil markets
  - geopolitical risk
  - analog forecasting
  - walk-forward validation
  - pre-registration
  - proper scoring rules
abstract: >-
  A corpus of 313 dated geopolitical and policy shocks (1973–2026), a world-state
  panel from seventeen open datasets joined under a vintage rule, a market-defined
  census of the largest oil-price moves, a state-conditioned analog engine reading
  each event as a frequency distribution over independently coded escalation
  outcomes (IES-90) and 20-day price paths, and a pre-registered walk-forward test
  with sealed reads, strictly proper scores, four baselines, and data-snooping,
  placebo, permutation, regime and specification-curve controls. The engine has no
  skill beyond the base rate on either target (run walk_20260902T182828Z); the
  null is published as computed.
references:
  - type: report
    title: "Does the record predict? A pre-registered walk-forward test of history-conditioned reads of geopolitical shocks in the oil economy"
    authors:
